# Several subjects for one (predicate, object), for get_mary_likes_matt_05.
# The decisive node comes first: ex:w shares the OBJECT but not the
# predicate, so a lookup that ignored the predicate would return it.
# ex:dupA and ex:dupB share (ex:certainty, 0.6): g.value returns the first
# the store yields (any=True), and so must .first() -- not the last, and no
# error.  ex:z carries 0.5 under another lexical form ("0.50"): g.value
# matches terms, not values, so a lookup for "0.5" finds nothing here.
@prefix ex:  <http://example.org/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

ex:w    ex:weight    0.6 .
ex:dupA ex:certainty 0.6 .
ex:dupB ex:certainty 0.6 .
ex:z    ex:certainty "0.50"^^xsd:decimal .
